## Probes 11 and 12 — the c8828d2 simplify fold (#130 retroactive r11)

Added under #130. The retroactive r11 review found that this log carried no
break/fail/restore probe for `c8828d2`, the post-convergence simplify fold — the
only round after correctness convergence that changed migration and derivation
code. Its closing tally at the top of this log still read `39 files, 1030
tests`, the PRE-fold
count, which is itself proof the log was never re-run after the fold. Both probes
below were run against the working tree during the #130 fix-forward, i.e. on
`985ed1c` plus that uncommitted fold -- NOT on `985ed1c` alone. The per-probe
counts reflect the tree at the moment each probe ran, which is why probe 11's
focused file shows 29 cases and probe 12's restore shows 1141: both predate the
deletion of the dead `migrateV4` test later in the same fold.

Method note: each mutation must COMPILE, or its RED is a type error rather than a
behavioural difference. The first attempt at probe 11 did not — swapping to
`TIER_TABLE` without adding the import produced `TS2304: Cannot find name
'TIER_TABLE'` and failed 21 tests, which looks stronger than the real probe and
means nothing. `tsc -b` exit status is captured directly below, not through a
pipe, because `$?` after a pipeline reports the last command in the pipe.

### Probe 11 — extraction transport must read `catalog.tiers`, not the global table

Break (note the added import, so the mutant type-checks):

```diff
 import { Fraction } from "../core/fraction.ts";
+import { TIER_TABLE } from "../data/tiers.ts";
@@ function transportForOutput
-  const tiers = catalog.tiers[kind];
+  const tiers = TIER_TABLE[kind];
```

```text
npx tsc -b   → tsc_exit=0
```

RED (`npx vitest run src/ui/extraction-plan.test.ts`, vitest_exit=1):

```text
FAIL  src/ui/extraction-plan.test.ts > deriveExtractionPlan > uses the catalog tier table for extractor transport
AssertionError: expected { status: 'requires-unlock', …(2) } to match object { status: 'available', …(2) }
Tests  1 failed | 28 passed (29)
```

Exactly one test fails, and it is the regression the fold added. Restore, then:

```text
Tests  29 passed (29)   (vitest_exit=0)
```

